{% extends "../layout.njk" %}
{% block headStylesheets %}
<link rel="preload" as="style" href="/pages/lune-and-wild.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/pages/lune-and-wild.css">
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Lune & Wild Header.svg" style="padding: 2vw 8vw;">
<img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Linkedin_Comp.gif" style="padding: 2vw 8vw;">
<div class="overview">
    <br/>
    <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Overview.svg">
    <p>
        <br/><br/>
        This is a self-initiated motion design
        exploration based on the existing brand identity
        created by Wild People Studio.
    </p><br />
    <p>
        Having followed the identity for some time, I
        wanted to explore how its visual language could
        translate into motion, using the project as an
        opportunity to experiment with movement,
        composition, and the relationship between
        static brand elements and animation.
    </p><br />
    <p>
        With no client brief or predefined deliverables,
        the project gave me the freedom to develop my
        own creative directon while strengthening my
        approach to brand-led motion design. It was
        also an opportunity to explore Cavalry more
        deeply and experiment with techniques I could
        carry into future identity and motion projects
    </p><br />
    <p>
        <b>Brand Identity:</b> Wild People Studio <br />
        <b>Motion Design:</b> Me
    </p>
</div>
<div class="gallery">
    <div class="gallery-item">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Logo_Anim_G&Y_2.gif">
    </div>
    <div class="gallery-item">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Challenging Myself.svg">
        <p>
            This project was primarily an opportunity to challenge myself as a motion designer.
        </p><br />
        <p>
            Rather than starting with a client brief or a defined set of requirements, I set myself the challenge of
            taking an
            existing brand identity and finding a way to extend its visual language through motion without compromising
            what made the identity work in the first place.
        </p><br />
        <p>
            I wanted to push myself to think beyond simply animating individual elements and instead consider how
            movement could become part of the brand expression itself — exploring rhythm, timing, transitions and
            composition to create something that felt intentional and connected to the original identity.
        </p><br />
        <p>
            I also used the project as an opportunity to step further outside my usual workflow and get more comfortable
            working in Cavalry. With no client constraints or expectations, I could experiment, make mistakes and
            iterate freely,
            using the project as a space to develop new techniques and broaden my motion design toolkit.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="gallery-item">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Finding a Solution.svg">
        <p>
            I approached the project by looking closely at the existing identity and identifying the visual
            characteristics that
            could naturally translate into motion. Rather than introducing a completely new visual language, I wanted
            the
            animation to feel like an extension of the brand itself.
        </p><br />
        <p>
            I explored how the identity's shapes, typography and graphic elements could move, interact and transition
            between one another. This became less about adding movement for the sake of it and more about finding a
            consistent motion language that felt playful, considered and true to the original design.
        </p><br />
        <p>
            Through experimentation and iteration in Cavalry, I developed a series of transitions and behaviours that
            allowed
            the individual brand elements to work together as a cohesive sequence. The result was a motion concept that
            builds on the existing identity while giving it a new dimension through movement.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="gallery-item quad-wrapper">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Basket_Comp.gif" class="quad">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Pork_Ragu.gif" class="quad">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/Cheesy_Sauce_with_Hidden_Veg.gif" class="quad">
        <img src="/assets/projects/lune-and-wild/World_Flavours.gif" class="quad">
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}